    Then ${\mathfrak p}, {\mathfrak p}'' \in {\mathfrak C}_4(k,n,j)$ by \eqref{defc5}, and thus by \Cref{C4-convex} ${\mathfrak p}' \in {\mathfrak C}_4(k,n,j)$.
    It suffices to show that if ${\mathfrak p}' \in {\mathfrak L}_4(k,n,j)$ then ${\mathfrak p}\in {\mathfrak L}_4(k,n,j)$ by contraposition;
